## 0. Summary & locked decisions

**Feature 1: Setup.** Add a new project-settings side-nav item, **"Cybernetics Data"**, at
`/<workspaceSlug>/settings/projects/<projectId>/cybernetics-data`. A project admin enters:

| Field (UI label) | Meaning | Storage |
|---|---|---|
| `CYBERNETICS_DATA_URL` | Origin of the Cybernetics-Data deployment (its `PUBLIC_ORIGIN`), e.g. `https://data.example.com` | plaintext, normalised |
| `CYBERNETICS_APITOKEN` | A Cybernetics-Data personal access token (`cybernetics_<id>_<sig>`) | **Fernet-encrypted**, write-only |

**Feature 2: Select.** In the work-item detail view (peek overview and full page), a new **"Database"** button sits next to
*Add sub-work item / Add relation / Add link / Attach*. It opens a modal where the user can:
- browse **Space → Base ("database") → Table**;
- query records (search, view, filter, sort, paginate);
- select records and attach them to the work item;
- view a single record in detail.

Attached records then appear in a **"Database records"** collapsible under the other widgets.

**Locked decisions** (reasons in §1–§3):

1. **The Plane backend is a server-side proxy.** The browser never sees the token and never calls Cybernetics-Data directly.
   The token must stay secret, the Data-Centre may sit on a private network, and this keeps one auth model.
2. **"Database" = Teable Base.** Space is an optional grouping level above it. Teable's `db-connection` feature (raw Postgres
   DSN) is **not** used (§1.1).
3. **Configuration is per project.** It lives in a new table `project_cybernetics_data_integrations`, one active row per project.
4. **Attached records are stored as references plus a display snapshot.** New table `issue_cybernetics_records`, holding
   ids + record name + table/base names + deep link. Plane never copies full record data. Live data is always fetched through
   the proxy.
5. **Every outbound call goes through `pinned_fetch`** (`P/apps/api/plane/utils/url_security.py:198`), the existing
   SSRF-safe client. A dedicated allowlist, `CYBERNETICS_DATA_ALLOWED_HOSTS/IPS`, permits private-network deployments.
6. **Frontend changes go into the CE extension points** (`apps/web/ce/...` stubs and `routes/extended.ts`) where possible,
   to keep core diffs small and merges from upstream Plane easy.

**Product decisions confirmed 2026-09-23 (v1):**

| # | Decision | Effect on this design |
|---|---|---|
| D1 | **Shared project token.** Every project member (Member/Admin) browses Cybernetics-Data with the permissions of the one token the project admin configured. There are no per-user tokens in v1. | §5.2 one integration row per project; §5.7 delegation warning shown in settings; per-user tokens deferred (§10 Q4). |
| D2 | **Guests see only saved previews.** They can see attached records' snapshots, but can't browse, open the live record viewer, attach or refresh. | §5.7 matrix; §6.7 guest rows are static (no click-to-view, no ↗ deep link needed beyond the stored `source_url`). |
| D3 | **Work items only.** No epics and no intake items in v1. | §6.4 button hidden unless `issueServiceType === ISSUES`; backend routes under `issues/…` only. |
| D4 | **Read-only.** Nothing is written back to Cybernetics-Data. | Client exposes GET methods only; token needs read scopes only (§1.2). |

