## 4. Architecture overview

```
┌──────────────────────── Browser (apps/web) ────────────────────────┐
│ Settings › Cybernetics Data         Work item › [Database] button   │
│  (URL + token form, Test)           → CyberneticsDataBrowserModal   │
│                                     → "Database records" widget     │
└───────────────┬───────────────────────────────┬────────────────────┘
                │ session cookie (same as all Plane app calls)
                ▼                               ▼
┌──────────────────────── Plane Django API ──────────────────────────┐
│ app/views/cybernetics_data/                                        │
│   config.py   ── ProjectCyberneticsDataIntegration (encrypted token)│
│   browse.py   ── read-only proxy (spaces/bases/tables/fields/views/ │
│                  records/record)          + throttle + short cache  │
│   records.py  ── IssueCyberneticsRecord CRUD + issue_activity       │
│ utils/cybernetics_data/                                             │
│   client.py   ── CyberneticsDataClient (pinned_fetch, timeouts,     │
│                  error mapping, param serialisation)                │
│   service.py  ── config lookup, decrypt, cache, snapshot builder    │
└───────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                │ HTTPS, Authorization: Bearer cybernetics_<id>_<sig>
                ▼
┌──────────────── Cybernetics-Data (NestJS /api/*) ──────────────────┐
│ /api/space  /api/base/access/all  /api/base/{b}/table               │
│ /api/table/{t}/field|view|record  /api/table/{t}/record/{r}          │
│ /api/table/{t}/aggregation/row-count                                 │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

**Request flow when attaching records:**

1. The modal calls `GET …/cybernetics-data/tables/{tbl}/records?search=…` → Django → Data-Centre.
2. The user ticks rows → `POST …/issues/{id}/cybernetics-records/` with `[{base_id, table_id, record_id}]`.
3. Django re-fetches each record server-side. This checks that the table belongs to the base, the record exists and the token
   can read it. Django then stores the reference plus snapshot and queues `issue_activity`.
4. The widget re-renders from the returned rows, and activity refreshes.

