## 7. Security review

| Threat | Mitigation |
|---|---|
| Token disclosure | Fernet-encrypted at rest (§5.3); `write_only` in the serializer; only `token_hint` is returned; never logged or placed in activity/errors; not sent to the browser; stripped from exception context. |
| SSRF via `CYBERNETICS_DATA_URL` | Validated at write time (`validate_url`) **and** at every call (`pinned_fetch` re-resolves and pins the IP, blocks private/metadata ranges, no redirects, `trust_env=False`). Private deployments must be allowlisted explicitly (`CYBERNETICS_DATA_ALLOWED_HOSTS/IPS`). Only project admins can set the URL. |
| Path injection into upstream URLs | Strict id regexes with prefixes (`bse…`, `tbl…`, `rec…`, `viw…`, `fld…`) before URL building; ids are never concatenated unvalidated. |
| Filter abuse / expensive queries | Plane-side filter schema (operator allowlist, depth ≤ 3, ≤ 20 conditions); `take` ≤ 200; per-user/project throttle; 10 s timeout; 5 MB response cap. |
| Privilege delegation (members act with the admin's token) | Admin-only configuration; explicit warning in the UI; documented recommendation to use a dedicated service account with `spaceIds` restriction and read-only scopes; guests excluded from live browsing. |
| Cross-project leakage | Everything is keyed by `project_id` from the URL and checked by `allow_permission`; the cache key includes `project_id` + token fingerprint; the issue queryset checks active membership and a non-archived project. |
| XSS from external data | Every value is rendered as React text; no HTML/markdown rendering of external values; image URLs are restricted to http(s); external links use `rel="noopener noreferrer"`. |
| Accidental Plane logout | Upstream 401 is mapped to **424** so Plane's axios 401 interceptor isn't triggered. |
| Secret-key rotation | Decrypt failure → 409 `CYBERNETICS_TOKEN_UNREADABLE`; the UI prompts for re-entry. |
| Stale attachment/presigned URLs | Never persisted; only text previews are stored in snapshots. |

